      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789421415208,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Where sparse vectors can scale better",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Where sparse vectors can scale better",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RywnwQckyUgROXKEE1mbB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1707.0092050234477,
      "y": 217.98508596420288,
      "width": 810.2784423828125,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 89870690,
      "version": 272,
      "versionNonce": 1380904372,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789421415208,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Sparse retrieval uses an inverted index. At query time, the system visits posting\nlists only for the query’s active terms rather than comparing the query with every\ndocument.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis can be especially efficient when:\n\n- queries activate few terms;\n- document vectors remain highly sparse;\n- the collection has many documents but a manageable vocabulary;\n- the system needs exact lexical matching;\n- most computation runs efficiently on CPUs.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Sparse retrieval uses an inverted index. At query time, the system visits posting lists only for the query’s active terms rather than comparing the query with every document.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis can be especially efficient when:\n\n- queries activate few terms;\n- document vectors remain highly sparse;\n- the collection has many documents but a manageable vocabulary;\n- the system needs exact lexical matching;\n- most computation runs efficiently on CPUs.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
